---
// FeatureScript: Cadsense runs it locally, so the agent can test what it writes. The capture is the
// current app previewing a bolt-circle script on a plate: its inputs on the left, the six holes it
// cut, and the run's result along the bottom. It sits in the same tray as the hero's app window.
---

<section class="band" id="featurescript">
  <div class="frame">
    <div class="head">
      <h2><span>FeatureScript the agent can run.</span> It tests what it writes before anything touches Onshape.</h2>
      <p>
        Cadsense runs FeatureScript locally on Onshape's own standard library. Any <code>.fs</code> file in a
        project gets a live preview with Onshape-style inputs, and it updates right away.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure>
      <div class="tray">
        <img
          src="/landing/featurescript-preview-1200w.webp"
          srcset="/landing/featurescript-preview-1200w.webp 1200w, /landing/featurescript-preview-2400w.webp 2400w"
          sizes="(min-width: 1240px) 1104px, calc(100vw - 52px)"
          width="1200"
          height="720"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          alt="The Cadsense FeatureScript preview: a bolt-circle script with inputs for hole count, circle diameter and hole diameter, and a plate with six holes cut in it. The run reports OK."
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption>A bolt-circle script previewed on a plate. Pick a face and it cuts the holes.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  code {
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border: 1px solid var(--divide);
    border-radius: var(--round-chip);
    background: var(--elev);
    font: 13px var(--mono);
  }

  figure {
    margin: 56px 0 0;
  }

  .tray {
    padding: 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--divide);
    border-radius: var(--round-panel);
    background: var(--elev);
  }

  img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--round-card);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    figure {
      margin-top: 36px;
    }

    .tray {
      padding: 6px;
      border-radius: var(--round-card);
    }

    img {
      border-radius: var(--round-chip);
    }
  }
</style>
